  "body": "Part of #4023. Phase 1 of the path kernel. The design is in `docs/decisions/4024-path-kernel-design.md` (PR #4030).\n\nBlocked until the kernel crate skeleton is on `side/path-kernel`.\n\n## What to do\n\nMake Thread (the thread mill) plan through the path kernel (`camcraft-pathkernel`), behind the one switch. Deliver it as a sub-PR into `side/path-kernel`, not into `main`.\n\n- Write the recipe of Thread (the thread mill) in `camcraft-motion`: the choices for the six stages.\n- Guide: a helix (a curve with a depth per point).\n- Entry and exit: an arc lead from the bore centre (a cleared column). Else a refusal with a named reason.\n- Use the shared order, link, entry and exit stages. Add no ring, link or entry code of its own.\n- Do not change the old planner (`thread_ride.rs`). The old planner stays for the comparison until the switch-over.\n- Add the kind to the K7 law suite (#4027) and to the old-against-new comparison of the example catalog.\n\n## Done means\n\n- With the switch at new, Thread (the thread mill) plans through the kernel, and the K7 laws hold for it.\n- With the switch at old, the output is identical to `main`.\n- Each difference between old and new in the example catalog has a one-line reason.\n- The sub-PR ends with `Refs #N`. The issue closes with the switch-over PR.\n",
